--TEST--
`Core\Reflect\ClassInfo::construct` binds `$arguments` to the declared parameters in order, agreeing property for property with the `new` beside it, and a class declaring no constructor is built from its armed defaults — `rule:core-classes/reflect`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// What one `Core\Reflect\ClassInfo` builds is asked about here, not who is
// allowed to build it. The question is what the constructed instance *is*, as an
// agreement between the two doors rather than as one right-looking answer: an
// argument list bound in the wrong order, or a constructor body skipped, prints
// plausibly on its own and fails against the `new` written beside it.
class Crate {
    public string $label;
    public int $size;
    public string $stamp;

    public function constructor(string $label, int $size) {
        $this->label = $label;
        $this->size = $size;
        // Derived in the body, so a door that allocated and armed the defaults
        // without running the constructor answers the empty string here.
        $this->stamp = $label . "/" . ($size as string);
    }
}

// `rule:classes/definite-property-initialization` gives this class nothing to
// run, so the allocation with its declared defaults is the whole of its
// construction — and `$arguments` is still written, as `[]`.
class Marker {
    public int $count = 9;
    public string $note = "unset";
}

var $crate = Core\Reflect::forClass("Crate");
if ($crate == null) {
    echo "unreachable", "\n";
} else {
    mixed $reflective = $crate->construct(["disk", 3]);
    var $ordinary = new Crate("disk", 3);

    echo $crate->get($reflective, "label") == $ordinary->label ? "label agrees" : "label differs", "\n";
    echo $crate->get($reflective, "size") == $ordinary->size ? "size agrees" : "size differs", "\n";
    echo $crate->get($reflective, "stamp") == $ordinary->stamp ? "stamp agrees" : "stamp differs", "\n";
    echo "stamp: ", $crate->get($reflective, "stamp"), "\n";

    // The two are separate instances, not one object answered twice: a write
    // through one is not readable through the other.
    $crate->set($reflective, "label", "tape");
    echo $crate->get($reflective, "label"), " ", $ordinary->label, "\n";
}

var $marker = Core\Reflect::forClass("Marker");
if ($marker == null) {
    echo "unreachable", "\n";
} else {
    mixed $blank = $marker->construct([]);
    echo $marker->get($blank, "count"), " ", $marker->get($blank, "note"), "\n";
}
--EXPECT--
label agrees
size agrees
stamp agrees
stamp: disk/3
tape disk
9 unset
